1421: /*
1422: The module loading model under ASYNCIFY is convoluted. We need to make sure we
1423: never have an async request running concurrently for loading modules.
1424: 
1425: The first implemenation looked like this:
1426: 
1427: C                                  HOST                      SUSPENDED
1428: qts_host_load_module(name) ------>                            false
1429:                                    call rt.loadModule(name)   false
1430:                                    Start async load module    false
1431:                                    Suspend C                  true
1432:                                    Async load complete        true
1433:             < ---------------      QTS_CompileModule(source)  true
1434: QTS_Eval(source, COMPILE_ONLY)                                true
1435: Loaded module has import                                      true
1436: qts_host_load_module(dep) ------->                            true
1437:                                   call rt.loadModule(dep)     true
1438:                                   Start async load module     true
1439:                                   ALREADY SUSPENDED, CRASH
1440: 
1441: We can solve this in two different ways:
1442: 
1443: 1. Return to C as soon as we async load the module source.
1444:    That way, we unsuspend before calling QTS_CompileModule.
1445: 2. Once we load the module, use a new API to detect and async
1446:    load the module's downstream dependencies. This way
1447:    they're loaded synchronously so we don't need to suspend "again".
1448: 
1449: Probably we could optimize (2) to make it more performant, eg with parallel
1450: loading, but (1) seems much easier to implement in the sort run.
1451: */
